    {
      "contact_id": "agxzfnViZXItdm9pY2VyFAsSB0NvbnRhY3QYgMDCpa3_ogkM",
      "content": "Okay.",
      "name": "Jeanne Walker",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:32:48.643039",
      "type": "transcript"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, okay so I got it pulled up and yeah, I do remember you wanted to kind of get on the schedule for that day we have availability. I just wanna make sure that we're kind of getting you like booked onto the schedule appropriately. Like, we don't wanna like, over the situation for it looking like.",
      "name": "Lukas Konrad",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:32:51.430445",
      "type": "transcript",
      "user_id": "6549949337878528"
    },
    {
      "content": "call_purpose",
      "name": "Lukas Konrad",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:32:51.430445",
      "type": "moment",
      "user_id": "6549949337878528"
    },
    {
      "contact_id": "agxzfnViZXItdm9pY2VyFAsSB0NvbnRhY3QYgMDCpa3_ogkM",
      "content": "Yeah. Because when I was looking at the quote or the estimate it was definitely overbooked but that's because again like you said you need more details so let me, let you ask questions unless you want me to just explain the situation.",
      "name": "Jeanne Walker",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:33:09.043039",
      "type": "transcript"
    },
    {
      "content": "ai_scorecard_llm_v2",
      "name": "Lukas Konrad",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:33:09.043445",
      "type": "moment",
      "user_id": "6549949337878528"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, you could just explain the situation I could kind of throw my questions in when they come up.",
      "name": "Lukas Konrad",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:33:24.430445",
      "type": "transcript",
      "user_id": "6549949337878528"
    },
    {
      "content": "ai_scorecard",
      "name": "Lukas Konrad",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:33:27.414445",
      "type": "moment",
      "user_id": "6549949337878528"
    },
    {
      "contact_id": "agxzfnViZXItdm9pY2VyFAsSB0NvbnRhY3QYgMDCpa3_ogkM",
      "content": "Okay. Alright. So it's not that I have a house full of furniture. I moved out of my apartment and and with someone who had a house. My I've got my boxes and my like my coffee table and my dresser are taking a half of the garage. I don't have an inventory at all. I can count the boxes but anyway, so it's just that taking it half the garage and then, and my bedroom I have you know my, my bed and then in a night stand, and then and I'll have my, my stuff in my closet, like my cloth and all that stuff. I'll already have that done actually. I'm just gonna leave it because I'm not moving out that same day for taking all the stuff to a storage unit.",
      "name": "Jeanne Walker",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:33:28.843039",
      "type": "transcript"
    },
    {
      "contact_id": "agxzfnViZXItdm9pY2VyFAsSB0NvbnRhY3QYgMDCpa3_ogkM",
      "content": "And, and then let's see in downstairs is okay, so my bed and the night stand are upstairs but it's just it's just those two items.",
      "name": "Jeanne Walker",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:34:19.243039",
      "type": "transcript"
    },
    {
      "contact_id": "agxzfnViZXItdm9pY2VyFAsSB0NvbnRhY3QYgMDCpa3_ogkM",
      "content": "And then downstairs I have my kitchen table with four chairs. Yeah, full chairs and and then I have my sofa, that's one of those electronic recliners, but I will, I'll try to already have, have it the back taken off cause they just kinda clip in but if I don't then, do they know how to do that?",
      "name": "Jeanne Walker",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:34:34.843039",
      "type": "transcript"
    },
    {
      "content": "Yeah. It's something we see fairly frequently. So it shouldn't be like out of the ordinary to see like, you know, that so most guys I would assume have seen that situation for, unless like, you know, first week here, kind of situation.",
      "name": "Lukas Konrad",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:35:01.030445",
      "type": "transcript",
      "user_id": "6549949337878528"
    },
    {
      "contact_id": "agxzfnViZXItdm9pY2VyFAsSB0NvbnRhY3QYgMDCpa3_ogkM",
      "content": "Yeah. Okay. So, so it's just that, I mean, I do have some boxes downstairs in that front room where my table is but, but you all aren't gonna move those, so I'll definitely have to be here to, to point out what to take and since they don't take any of their stuff, but the stuff that's in the, my boxes that are in front room, that's my, I don't know my, like, my, my pictures, my personal family pictures and things, and I'm gonna move those myself in my car. So, so that's it. I mean, it's, I really think and, and we're just taking to a storage unit, which is literally just down the street.",
      "name": "Jeanne Walker",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:35:14.443039",
      "type": "transcript"
    },
    {
      "contact_id": "agxzfnViZXItdm9pY2VyFAsSB0NvbnRhY3QYgMDCpa3_ogkM",
      "content": "So, if I have everything ready, I really think we could probably get it done within that two hours. If it goes over I would be surprised.",
      "name": "Jeanne Walker",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:35:59.443039",
      "type": "transcript"
    },
    {
      "content": "Yeah it sounds very straightforward and simple. Main variable I would say is in play would be like the box count give or take, for like a, like, sounds like it's like a one bedroom equivalent kind of situation. Those we typically see like you know, fifteen to 25 boxes if it's like a higher box, yeah, maybe it'll take a little bit longer but it does sound like we're probably gonna be like middle to lower end of that spectrum. So, I do think like this is very straightforward, very simple and standard on the day I think it would fall anywhere between that two and a half hour minimum and if it does go a little bit over maybe three hours but that's kind of pushing it realistically speaking. Cause unloads into storage are typically pretty quick and honestly and like load ups the main.",
      "name": "Lukas Konrad",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:36:09.430445",
      "type": "transcript",
      "user_id": "6549949337878528"
    },
    {
      "content": "ai_scorecard_llm_v2",
      "name": "Lukas Konrad",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:36:09.430445",
      "type": "moment",
      "user_id": "6549949337878528"
    },
    {
      "content": "monologuing",
      "name": "Lukas Konrad",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:36:35.934445",
      "type": "moment",
      "user_id": "6549949337878528"
    },
    {
      "content": "Time. Yeah, the main thing that's gonna take time would just be wrapping the items. So they're ready to go on the day of so I think two and a half to three hours is a lot more of a share estimate for the move. Two and a half hours would be our minimum charge which would be $480 for a two man crew and then the event it does go up to three hours, it'd be $576 we have that two F. our minimum. And then everything else after that gets billed in fifteen minute increments so you do only pay for the time that does get used on the day of. So ultimately if it does go over two and a half hours like $245 or $315 or something like that, that's how, what you pay for. So the estimate is not set in stone but as I mentioned I think the minimum is pretty doable in this situation. I just don't like to make promises, I can't keep.",
      "name": "Lukas Konrad",
      "time": "2026-09-12T18:36:54.430445",
      "type": "transcript",
      "user_id": "6549949337878528"
    },
